<BaseLayout title="Responsible Disclosure | Sparaton Studios"><section class="shell hero"><div><p class="eyebrow">Responsible disclosure</p><h1>Found a security problem? Tell us without publishing someone else’s data.</h1></div><p class="lede">Use the Contact route for security reports until a dedicated security address is confirmed.</p></section><section class="section"><article class="shell prose"><h2>What helps</h2><p>Include the affected URL or component, reproducible steps, expected versus observed behavior, and enough technical detail to investigate safely.</p><h2>Please avoid</h2><p>Do not intentionally access other clients' ticket content, download private data, degrade the service, send spam, or publicly disclose an unresolved issue that could put users at immediate risk.</p><h2>No invented program terms</h2><p>This page does not promise a bounty, compensation, legal safe harbor, or response deadline. Any formal vulnerability-disclosure policy should be reviewed before those commitments are made.</p></article></section></BaseLayout>
